tion with Veratrum preparations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Concurrent use of 胆胃康 and 藜芦及其制剂 (Veratrum and its preparations) is contraindicated. In traditional Chinese medicine theory, Veratrum (Li Lu) is considered incompatible with many herbs due to opposing pharmacological actions or toxicity potentiation. This interaction warning highlights the importance of screening for concomitant herbal product use when prescribing or recommending Danweikang, especially in integrative or outpatient settings where polypharmacy with traditional remedies is common. [Data: Relationships (48866); Entities (8057, 11797)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Monitoring of liver function is recommended during cefmenoxime therapy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Clinical guidance for 注射用盐酸头孢甲肟 advises periodic monitoring of liver function, along with renal function and blood parameters, during treatment. This precaution reflects potential hepatotoxicity or the drug’s metabolic burden on the liver, particularly in prolonged or high-dose regimens. While no specific adverse event is detailed beyond vitamin K deficiency, the recommendation underscores the need for vigilance in patients with pre-existing hepatic impairment or those receiving multiple hepatotoxic agents. [Data: Relationships (2875); Entities (6529)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community presents moderate-to-high clinical impact due to the critical role of its antibiotics in treating severe infections, coupled with significant safety considerations including drug incompatibilities, adverse reactions, and herb-drug interactions.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782128028, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "syste